# .sanitize-ignore — explicit whitelist for release-sanitize.sh (S3-1)
#
# Format: one path (relative to scanned root) per line; '#' starts comment; blank OK.
# Paths are matched via case glob against the relative file path.
#
# Rule of thumb: only add entries you can defend in a security review.
# Prefer fixing the source over adding a line here.

# ── Intentional test fixtures ────────────────────────────────────────────
# These files carry planted patterns so the scanner's detectors can be tested.
# They are self-documenting test data; the strings are not real credentials.
tests/test_sanitize.sh
tests/test_no_force_bypass.sh
tests/test_credential_patterns.sh
tests/test_sanitize_ignore_hardening.sh
tests/test_sanitize_output_format.sh

# v1.13.0: marketplace BDD fixtures (intentional sample plugin entries, NOT live data)
tests/fixtures/marketplace*.json
tests/fixtures/plugin-entry-*.json

# ── Business contact (by design, not a leak) ─────────────────────────────
# SECURITY.md intentionally exposes a real contact email so reporters can
# reach maintainers. Not a secret.
SECURITY.md

# ── Internal dev docs (gitignored, never shipped) ────────────────────────
# These files are listed in .gitignore and excluded by release.sh rsync —
# they never enter a release artifact. Whitelisted here only so that
# `release-sanitize.sh .` (local self-check on repo root) exits clean.
.omc/*
.superpowers/*
REVIEW.md
GitHub_STANDARD_ANALYSIS.md
HANDOFF.md
HANDOFF.archive.md
HANDOFF.md.bak
HANDOFF.md.pre-v2-backup
GOTCHAS.md
Handoff_Logs/*
Handoff_Decisions/*
Handoff_Logs.archive/*
# handoffx v4 (2026-11) renamed the set to HANDOFFX.md / Handoffx_*; both
# generations stay listed because stale tarballs and backups still carry the old names.
HANDOFFX.md
HANDOFFX.archive.md
HANDOFFX.md.bak
HANDOFFX.md.pre-v2-backup
Handoffx_Logs/*
Handoffx_Decisions/*
Handoffx_Logs.archive/*
# gitx-sop per-release publish worktree (own .git, public-mirror only):
# gitignored + release.sh --exclude'd; whitelisted so a whole-repo
# self-check stays clean while the worktree transiently exists.
.github-publish-wt/*
# pyenv local pin (codex P2, v1.9.6): gitignored + release.sh --exclude'd;
# listed here so the whole-repo self-check stays clean (five-facet parity).
.python-version
# graphify knowledge graph + local Claude instruction: gitignored +
# release.sh --exclude'd. graphify-out/ is built from the private
# working-memory set above; CLAUDE.md is local Claude Code instruction.
# Whitelisted so a whole-repo self-check stays clean (same parity).
CLAUDE.md
graphify-out/*

# ── superpowers spec/plan docs (internal design records) ─────────────────
# Tracked by git for cross-machine sync (Syncthing) but never enter the
# source tarball or .skill bundle (release.sh rsync excludes docs/super-).
# Contain a placeholder security-contact email and Co-Authored-By
# signatures (Anthropic's noreply identity) that are documentation, not real PII.
docs/superpowers/specs/*
docs/superpowers/plans/*

# ── Syncthing conflict quarantine (.gitignored) ──────────────────────────
.syncthing-quarantine-*/*

# ── gitx-sop SOP template (intentional git-identity literal) ─────────────
# GitHub's noreply address is its reserved non-routable identity used in the
# generated SOP's `git config user.email` step — documentation, not PII.
# Template is de-hardcoded (placeholders only), TDD-guarded, reviewed.
references/gitx-sop/*
skills/gitx-release/references/gitx-sop/*

# ── Generated release artifacts (not source input) ───────────────────────
# release.sh scans the staged source and the fresh .skill bundle separately.
# Historical Release/* outputs are ignored for whole-repo local self-checks.
Release/*

# .gitx/ policy pack (GITHUB_RELEASE_SOP.md, marketplace-entry.json, …):
# gitignored + release.sh --exclude'd private working memory (CLAUDE.md).
# Its `git config user.email` (GitHub's noreply address) is the SOP's documented
# public-safe publish identity, never shipped. Whitelisted so the whole-repo
# self-check stays clean — same class as .github-publish-wt/* / .omc/*.
.gitx/*

# ── gitx-marketplace helper (intentional git-identity literal) ───────────
# scripts/gitx-marketplace.sh sets `git config user.email` to GitHub's noreply address
# on its mktemp clone of the marketplace repo to author register/bump PRs —
# the SAME GitHub-reserved non-routable identity used by the gitx-sop SOP
# template (allowlisted above for references/gitx-sop/*). v1.13.0 ships a
# 16-assertion BDD suite (test_gitx_marketplace.sh) and 12-assertion wrapper
# hook suite (test_gitx_release_marketplace_hook.sh) that exercise these
# code paths, so a real PII regression would be caught upstream of release.
scripts/gitx-marketplace.sh
skills/gitx-release/scripts/gitx-marketplace.sh
